<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 11 January, from 630 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mecca" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mecca.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">630 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,396 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Muhammad enters Mecca and clears the Kaaba of idols</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By the usual reckoning, Muhammad and some 10,000 followers took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> with little bloodshed. The idols around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaaba">Kaaba</a> were destroyed and it was rededicated as the centre of Islamic worship.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1158 CE <span class="tih-ago">868 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vladislaus II becomes King of Bohemia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> granted Duke Vladislaus II a royal crown in return for support in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. He was crowned at Regensburg, only the second Bohemian ruler to hold the title of king.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1569 CE <span class="tih-ago">457 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">England's first recorded state lottery is drawn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chartered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> to raise money for harbours and public works, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s first state lottery was drawn at the west door of St Paul's Cathedral. Ticket holders were promised immunity from arrest for minor crimes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1787 CE <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Herschel discovers Titania and Oberon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Six years after finding Uranus, Herschel spotted its two largest moons. They were later named after the king and queen of the fairies in Shakespeare's 'A Midsummer Night's Dream'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1861 CE <span class="tih-ago">165 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alabama secedes from the Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a>'s convention voted 61 to 39 to leave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the fourth state to secede. Its capital Montgomery hosted the founding of the Confederate States the next month.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1922 CE <span class="tih-ago">104 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Insulin is first given to a diabetic patient</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fourteen-year-old Leonard Thompson received an insulin extract at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toronto">Toronto</a> General Hospital. The first dose failed, but a purer extract made by James Collip saved his life later that month.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1935 CE <span class="tih-ago">91 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Amelia Earhart sets out on the first solo flight from Hawaii</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Earhart took off from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a> and landed in Oakland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, about 18 hours later. She became the first person to fly solo across this stretch of the Pacific, some 3,900 km.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1946 CE <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albania proclaimed a People's Republic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Albania's assembly abolished the monarchy and declared a People's Republic under communist leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha">Enver Hoxha</a>. His regime became one of the most isolated and repressive in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1964 CE <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Surgeon General reports that smoking causes cancer</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Luther Terry's advisory committee concluded that cigarette smoking causes lung cancer in men. The report led to health warnings on cigarette packets and decades of anti-smoking policy.</p></div></li></ol>
